### Security

- Never expose Gemini credentials in frontend bundles.
- Validate uploads by file size, extension, content type and actual parsing result as appropriate.
- Avoid executing untrusted text or HTML.
- Validate request payloads and scenario mutations on the backend.
- Avoid logging secrets or unnecessary sensitive document content.
- Configure access controls for persisted user data.
- Add rate limiting or reasonable protection for AI endpoints where practical.

### Accessibility

- Semantic HTML.
- Visible focus states.
- Form labels and useful validation messages.
- Sufficient color contrast.
- Keyboard-accessible navigation and controls.
- Textual explanations for charts and dependency graphs.
- Status labels that do not depend on color alone.

### Code quality

- TypeScript types rather than avoidable `any` usage.
- Small, reusable components.
- Clear separation between UI, business rules, AI services and persistence.
- Consistent formatting and linting.
- No dead navigation links, fake submit buttons, unresolved imports or avoidable console errors.
- No placeholder screens presented as finished features.

